# A blacklist, deliberately.
#
# The whitelist form (`*` then `!name`) is tempting for a small context, but
# its directory-recursion rules are subtle enough that two attempts at it both
# shipped an EMPTY /opt/demo-book — the image built, the container started, and
# the demo served a blank ledger. The context here is dominated by a 15MB
# binary anyway, so excluding a few KB of templates buys nothing worth a subtle
# rule. List what must not ship, and let everything else through.
*.yaml
*.yml
.dockerignore
